<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Feb 5.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Feb 5.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* National Foods A$1.50 (steady)</p>
<p>Food group said the sale of its NationalPak business would generate a book profit of about A$70 million.</p>
<p>* Coms21 A$0.55 (issue price)</p>
<p>High technology design group makes debut on Australian Stock Exchange at 2.00 p.m. (0300 GMT).</p>
<p>* News Corp A$6.75 (+.01)</p>
<p>Media giant attracting active investor interest ahead of half year results scheduled for Thursday.</p>
<p>* St George Bank A$7.83 (+.04)</p>
<p>Newly created entity holds it first annual meeting since merging with Advance Bank.</p>
<p>* National Australia Bank A$15.70 (-.17)</p>
<p>* Commonwealth Bank A$12.90 (-.05)</p>
<p>* Westpac A$7.49 (-.19)</p>
<p>* ANZ Bank $8.10 (-.06)</p>
<p>Reserve bank leaves interest rates unchanged after board meeting. Big banks could come under seling pressure again.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
